WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.126 --> 00:00:03.515
- He's an American
motivational speaker, author,

00:00:03.515 --> 00:00:05.265
and former television host.

00:00:05.265 --> 00:00:08.222
As a motivational speaker,
he uses a catch phrase,

00:00:08.222 --> 00:00:09.797
"It's possible."

00:00:09.797 --> 00:00:12.153
And encourages people
to chase their dreams.

00:00:12.153 --> 00:00:14.272
He was the host of the Les Brown Show.

00:00:14.272 --> 00:00:17.430
He's Les Brown and here are
his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.780
(rocket blastoff)

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.083
- I do a lot of training
for many corporations

00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:26.108
and I conduct sales seminars
and I've heard all kind of guys

00:00:26.108 --> 00:00:29.483
doing techniques and
training people techniques

00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:32.218
of how to close sales
and how to work within

00:00:32.218 --> 00:00:36.627
and begin to control the sale
and how to ask for the close.

00:00:36.627 --> 00:00:38.131
Let me share something with you.

00:00:38.131 --> 00:00:39.851
You can learn all the
techniques in the world.

00:00:39.851 --> 00:00:42.601
If you don't believe in yourself,

00:00:44.084 --> 00:00:46.685
it won't happen for you.

00:00:46.685 --> 00:00:49.014
I learned all of it.

00:00:49.014 --> 00:00:51.176
That's why I do a training
called Focus on the Seller.

00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:55.343
You've got to focus on you
and as you convince you,

00:00:56.188 --> 00:01:00.337
as you sell yourself every
day, every day, every day,

00:01:00.337 --> 00:01:02.560
you will begin to see a
difference in the things

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:03.909
that you're doing.

00:01:03.909 --> 00:01:06.898
Selling yourself on your
ability to perform a job,

00:01:06.898 --> 00:01:10.119
to achieve a certain objective,
telling yourself every day,

00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:14.135
"Here I go again and I got what it takes."

00:01:14.135 --> 00:01:18.544
"This is my day and nothing
out here is going to stop me."

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:21.812
It's necessary that you be flexible.

00:01:21.812 --> 00:01:23.494
That you are always thinking

00:01:23.494 --> 00:01:26.033
of how can I improve this better.

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.102
This is a customer-driven economy.

00:01:28.102 --> 00:01:31.141
It's necessary for you to
always explore various ways

00:01:31.141 --> 00:01:34.374
in which you can improve
the quality of service

00:01:34.374 --> 00:01:37.944
that you're providing for the
people in your organization.

00:01:37.944 --> 00:01:40.160
I remember something a major
company had talked about,

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.457
the extra value service
they were providing

00:01:42.457 --> 00:01:43.679
for their customers.

00:01:43.679 --> 00:01:45.615
And the lady who had the news conference

00:01:45.615 --> 00:01:47.109
summarized it this way.

00:01:47.109 --> 00:01:51.815
She said "It's not our intention
to satisfy our customers

00:01:51.815 --> 00:01:53.624
"or to please our customers.

00:01:53.624 --> 00:01:56.374
"Our intention is to amaze them."

00:01:57.323 --> 00:01:59.980
It's necessary if you're
going to compete today

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:03.804
that you look for ways
to amaze your customers

00:02:03.804 --> 00:02:06.207
by being one of those individuals that

00:02:06.207 --> 00:02:08.123
keep your commitments,
that keep your word,

00:02:08.123 --> 00:02:09.501
that's relentless.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:11.560
It's necessary as you work with the people

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.322
that you bring into your organization

00:02:14.322 --> 00:02:16.646
that they see that you are
a good example of a person

00:02:16.646 --> 00:02:19.887
to work with because you model
integrity, and determination,

00:02:19.887 --> 00:02:22.470
and ambition, and truth and honesty

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.376
in the way in which you conduct business.

00:02:25.376 --> 00:02:30.208
The other thing is take full
responsibility for your life.

00:02:30.208 --> 00:02:33.693
Accept where you are
and the responsibility

00:02:33.693 --> 00:02:36.149
that you're going to take
yourself where you want to go.

00:02:36.149 --> 00:02:38.631
Someone said we have two
primary choices in life.

00:02:38.631 --> 00:02:42.773
We can either accept
conditions as they exist,

00:02:42.773 --> 00:02:46.715
or we can take the
responsibility to change them.

00:02:46.715 --> 00:02:48.810
See a lot of people want
to exempt themselves

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.675
from taking responsibility.

00:02:50.675 --> 00:02:52.817
All they want to do is
talk about the problem.

00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:55.039
Every time you see them,
they'll tell you their story

00:02:55.039 --> 00:02:58.206
over and over and over and over again.

00:03:00.132 --> 00:03:00.965
No. No.

00:03:00.965 --> 00:03:03.707
You want to take
responsibility for your life.

00:03:03.707 --> 00:03:04.635
I got me here.

00:03:04.635 --> 00:03:07.044
I can get me out of this.

00:03:07.044 --> 00:03:08.711
And I'm getting out.

00:03:09.783 --> 00:03:13.687
I'm not going to be a volunteer victim.

00:03:13.687 --> 00:03:15.280
George Bernard Shaw
said there are two kinds

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.872
of people in life: those
that make things happen,

00:03:18.872 --> 00:03:20.543
those that watch things happen, and those

00:03:20.543 --> 00:03:23.043
that don't know what happened.

00:03:24.397 --> 00:03:25.847
And he said the people
that get along in this life

00:03:25.847 --> 00:03:28.158
look around for the
circumstances that they want

00:03:28.158 --> 00:03:30.749
and if they can't find 'em, they make 'em.

00:03:30.749 --> 00:03:32.505
They create 'em.

00:03:32.505 --> 00:03:34.521
So part of beginning to get unstuck,

00:03:34.521 --> 00:03:36.488
you've got to decide
that the behavior pattern

00:03:36.488 --> 00:03:39.359
that you have adopted
doesn't work for you.

00:03:39.359 --> 00:03:40.613
You've got to change your strategies

00:03:40.613 --> 00:03:44.780
and changing your strategy
means reinventing your life.

00:03:46.506 --> 00:03:50.171
Recreating you and you
have the power to do that.

00:03:50.171 --> 00:03:52.033
You can decide that
you're going to change,

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:54.700
that you're not going to be a wimp.

00:03:55.562 --> 00:03:59.729
You can decide that you're
going to stand up to life.

00:04:00.909 --> 00:04:03.228
You can decide that I'm
going to live each day

00:04:03.228 --> 00:04:05.061
as if it were my last.

00:04:06.128 --> 00:04:09.618
You have the power to make that decision.

00:04:09.618 --> 00:04:11.535
You can decide, "I'm
going to work on myself

00:04:11.535 --> 00:04:12.750
"and develop myself.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:14.917
"I'm going to empower me."

00:04:15.843 --> 00:04:18.970
And all of these things that
are happening to me right now,

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:21.779
they're just temporary inconveniences.

00:04:21.779 --> 00:04:23.787
They're not stronger than I am.

00:04:23.787 --> 00:04:24.928
I'm in charge here.

00:04:24.928 --> 00:04:28.538
Overcoming the negative
conversation, that inner dialogue

00:04:28.538 --> 00:04:31.788
that's going on all
the time, all the time.

00:04:31.788 --> 00:04:33.594
Even when you don't want it to be there.

00:04:33.594 --> 00:04:36.115
You can't stop yourself
right now from thinking.

00:04:36.115 --> 00:04:38.851
You can't do it. It's going on.

00:04:38.851 --> 00:04:41.783
And so learning how to empower yourself,

00:04:41.783 --> 00:04:46.223
part of doing that is
standing up to yourself.

00:04:46.223 --> 00:04:48.770
You've got to stand up
inside yourself sometimes

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:50.353
and say, "Shut up."

00:04:53.557 --> 00:04:55.761
You've got to do this.

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:58.183
I was going to give a
presentation, and this voice

00:04:58.183 --> 00:05:00.263
inside of me saying, "You can't do this.

00:05:00.263 --> 00:05:01.666
"You don't have everything it takes."

00:05:01.666 --> 00:05:03.166
I said, "Shut up."

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:07.813
I'm behind on my bills and you
telling me what I can't do.

00:05:07.813 --> 00:05:09.480
I have got to do it.

00:05:12.442 --> 00:05:14.767
You get scared sometimes.

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:16.582
Your mind will go blank on you.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:20.265
Some people you will allow to unnerve you.

00:05:20.265 --> 00:05:23.827
And you wonder, "What's wrong
with me, I'm not crazy."

00:05:23.827 --> 00:05:26.124
That's why you've got to
learn to make a conscious,

00:05:26.124 --> 00:05:30.134
deliberate, determined effort
to stand up inside yourself.

00:05:30.134 --> 00:05:32.459
Working on yourself,
watching that inner dialogue,

00:05:32.459 --> 00:05:34.865
it will determine the
quality of your life.

00:05:34.865 --> 00:05:35.800
Next thing is that you've got

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:38.501
to activate the thinker in you.

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:40.956
Don't allow your emotions to control you.

00:05:40.956 --> 00:05:42.929
We are emotional, but you want to begin

00:05:42.929 --> 00:05:45.789
to discipline your emotion.

00:05:45.789 --> 00:05:48.391
If you don't discipline
and contain your emotions,

00:05:48.391 --> 00:05:49.891
they will use you.

00:05:51.236 --> 00:05:53.790
Your mind goes on automatic,
just like a garden.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.076
You know I loved reading the book called

00:05:56.076 --> 00:05:58.101
As a Man Thinketh by James Allen.

00:05:58.101 --> 00:06:01.162
He uses the analogy of the
mind being like a garden.

00:06:01.162 --> 00:06:06.029
You know weeds don't have to
have any encouragement to grow.

00:06:06.029 --> 00:06:07.165
You don't have to water them.

00:06:07.165 --> 00:06:09.072
They don't have to get sunshine.

00:06:09.072 --> 00:06:10.592
They don't have to have fertile ground.

00:06:10.592 --> 00:06:14.006
They will grow through
the cracks of a sidewalk.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:14.839
Am I right?

00:06:14.839 --> 00:06:16.352
- [Audience] Yeah.

00:06:16.352 --> 00:06:20.121
- But if you want to grow
orchids or roses or any kind

00:06:20.121 --> 00:06:23.179
of exotic flowers, there
are special processes

00:06:23.179 --> 00:06:26.529
and procedures you must go through.

00:06:26.529 --> 00:06:29.776
By the same token, you
don't have to foss yourself

00:06:29.776 --> 00:06:33.979
or motivate yourself to think
negatively, to be depressed,

00:06:33.979 --> 00:06:36.374
to hate somebody, to want revenge,

00:06:36.374 --> 00:06:39.282
to want to get back at
somebody, to beat yourself up

00:06:39.282 --> 00:06:41.473
over the head, to feel loaded with guilt.

00:06:41.473 --> 00:06:44.291
You don't have to make
any effort to do that.

00:06:44.291 --> 00:06:45.923
Your mind is on automatic.

00:06:45.923 --> 00:06:48.090
It will do that by itself.

00:06:49.892 --> 00:06:51.224
But if you want to begin to move

00:06:51.224 --> 00:06:53.011
into your own personal greatness,

00:06:53.011 --> 00:06:54.490
if you want to begin to really

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:57.865
enjoy a happy successful healthy life,

00:06:57.865 --> 00:07:00.205
you've got to be willing
to go against the tide.

00:07:00.205 --> 00:07:03.895
You've got to be willing
to harness your will.

00:07:03.895 --> 00:07:07.895
And say, "In spite of
this, I'm in control here.

00:07:08.836 --> 00:07:10.367
"I'm not going to let this get me down.

00:07:10.367 --> 00:07:14.055
"I'm not going to let this destroy me.

00:07:14.055 --> 00:07:17.106
"I'm coming back and I'll
be stronger and better

00:07:17.106 --> 00:07:18.250
"because of it."

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.125
You have got to make a declaration

00:07:20.125 --> 00:07:23.055
that this is what you stand for.

00:07:23.055 --> 00:07:25.557
You're standing up for your dreams.

00:07:25.557 --> 00:07:27.185
You're standing up for peace of mind.

00:07:27.185 --> 00:07:29.685
You're standing up for health.

00:07:30.559 --> 00:07:34.859
You want it and you're going
to go all out to have it.

00:07:34.859 --> 00:07:36.534
It's not going to be easy.

00:07:36.534 --> 00:07:38.508
When you want a change, it's not easy.

00:07:38.508 --> 00:07:41.269
If it were in fact easy,
everybody would do it.

00:07:41.269 --> 00:07:43.393
But if you're serious, you'll go all out.

00:07:43.393 --> 00:07:45.335
I don't care how good you are,

00:07:45.335 --> 00:07:46.814
I don't care how talented you are,

00:07:46.814 --> 00:07:49.262
I don't care how much
you work on yourself,

00:07:49.262 --> 00:07:52.338
there's some times when things
aren't going to go right.

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:54.348
They just are not going to go right.

00:07:54.348 --> 00:07:57.369
There are times when anything
that can happen will happen.

00:07:57.369 --> 00:08:00.197
Murphy's Law will be
knocking at your door.

00:08:00.197 --> 00:08:01.989
Why? I don't know why.

00:08:01.989 --> 00:08:03.572
That's called life.

00:08:05.957 --> 00:08:08.496
And you have to deal with it.

00:08:08.496 --> 00:08:11.772
Sometimes your life will be in a slump.

00:08:11.772 --> 00:08:13.697
Just like sports.

00:08:13.697 --> 00:08:15.559
Some of the best shooters
can't hit baskets

00:08:15.559 --> 00:08:17.415
different times in games.

00:08:17.415 --> 00:08:18.421
They get in a slump.

00:08:18.421 --> 00:08:19.800
Do they sit on the sideline and say,

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:22.030
"You know I just didn't
hit a basket today."

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:22.913
No.

00:08:22.913 --> 00:08:25.225
They continue to execute.

00:08:25.225 --> 00:08:27.681
I suggest to you that if
you are facing a challenge,

00:08:27.681 --> 00:08:29.375
don't stop.

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:32.137
Stay busy. Work your plan.

00:08:32.137 --> 00:08:34.749
Continue to do those things
that you know that work for you

00:08:34.749 --> 00:08:38.385
after you have evaluated
yourself from the situation.

00:08:38.385 --> 00:08:39.472
Continue to move.

00:08:39.472 --> 00:08:41.967
Stay busy, stay busy, stay busy.

00:08:41.967 --> 00:08:45.232
I was working on a job
and I came home one day.

00:08:45.232 --> 00:08:47.536
I was married at the time
and I told my former wife,

00:08:47.536 --> 00:08:51.026
"That guy Burt I work for is stupid."

00:08:51.026 --> 00:08:52.494
She said, "If he's so stupid, why does

00:08:52.494 --> 00:08:54.430
he sign your paycheck?"

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.058
Now you see why I divorced her, right.

00:08:57.058 --> 00:09:00.058
(audience laughing)

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:03.691
I couldn't stand her.

00:09:06.634 --> 00:09:09.467
That night I could not sleep well.

00:09:10.511 --> 00:09:14.552
Here was a guy that was
controlling my life.

00:09:14.552 --> 00:09:16.138
I was going through all kind of changes

00:09:16.138 --> 00:09:19.471
because this man controlled my paycheck.

00:09:20.701 --> 00:09:24.497
And it was Carlisle who
said, "Truth crushed to earth

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:26.054
"shall rise again."

00:09:26.054 --> 00:09:28.512
Winston Churchill said, "The
truth is incontrovertible.

00:09:28.512 --> 00:09:31.312
"Malice may attack it,
ignorance may deride it

00:09:31.312 --> 00:09:33.561
"but at the end there it is."

00:09:33.561 --> 00:09:35.542
And we know Scripture that
says, "Ye shall know the truth

00:09:35.542 --> 00:09:39.204
"and the truth shall set you free."

00:09:39.204 --> 00:09:42.670
And the truth that I had
to come to grips with

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:45.486
that I wasn't in charge of my destiny.

00:09:45.486 --> 00:09:49.815
The truth was that I wasn't
giving all that I had.

00:09:49.815 --> 00:09:52.550
The truth was that there are
some things that I wanted to do

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:56.260
but I didn't have the courage
to act on those things.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:10:00.146
And the truth was that Burt
Childs was a blessing to me.

00:10:00.146 --> 00:10:02.187
He made life so miserable for me,

00:10:02.187 --> 00:10:05.844
I had to start looking
at my life differently.

00:10:05.844 --> 00:10:08.409
I started going to work earlier.

00:10:08.409 --> 00:10:10.802
I started being the
last one to leave there.

00:10:10.802 --> 00:10:13.720
I started working harder
than anybody else.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.645
The other guys could not, "Why
would you work so hard, Les?"

00:10:16.645 --> 00:10:18.445
I said, "I'm not working for them."

00:10:18.445 --> 00:10:21.784
I had been cheating Burt, I thought.

00:10:21.784 --> 00:10:23.899
I'd been cheating myself and my family.

00:10:23.899 --> 00:10:25.389
Wherever you are, whatever you're doing,

00:10:25.389 --> 00:10:27.614
do it with everything that you have.

00:10:27.614 --> 00:10:32.287
Develop the habit of giving
more than what you're paid for.

00:10:32.287 --> 00:10:34.348
Develop the habit of setting standards

00:10:34.348 --> 00:10:36.299
that others will be measured by.

00:10:36.299 --> 00:10:38.695
Someone said, "Do not go
where the path may lead,

00:10:38.695 --> 00:10:42.412
"but go where there's no
path and leave a trail."

00:10:42.412 --> 00:10:46.447
In the process of working on your dreams,

00:10:46.447 --> 00:10:51.024
you are going to incur
a lot of disappointment,

00:10:51.024 --> 00:10:55.191
a lot of failure, a lot of
pain, a lot of setbacks,

00:10:56.233 --> 00:10:57.646
a lot of defeats.

00:10:57.646 --> 00:11:01.337
But in the process of doing
that, you will discover

00:11:01.337 --> 00:11:05.522
some things about yourself
that you don't know right now.

00:11:05.522 --> 00:11:09.356
What you will realize is that
you have greatness within you.

00:11:09.356 --> 00:11:12.272
What you will realize is
that you are more powerful

00:11:12.272 --> 00:11:15.681
than you can ever begin to imagine.

00:11:15.681 --> 00:11:18.070
What you will realize
is that you are greater

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:20.208
than your circumstances,
that you don't have

00:11:20.208 --> 00:11:23.314
to go through life being a victim.

00:11:23.314 --> 00:11:25.348
As Jack indicated, I was
born in Miami, Florida,

00:11:25.348 --> 00:11:29.397
in an area called Liberty
City in an abandoned building

00:11:29.397 --> 00:11:33.230
on a hard linoleum floor
with my twin brother.

00:11:34.194 --> 00:11:36.832
We were six weeks of age we were adopted.

00:11:36.832 --> 00:11:39.695
When I was in fifth grade,
I was identified as EMR,

00:11:39.695 --> 00:11:42.054
labeled educable mentally retarded,

00:11:42.054 --> 00:11:45.273
put back from the fifth
grade into the fourth grade

00:11:45.273 --> 00:11:48.998
and stayed in that category
until I got out of high school.

00:11:48.998 --> 00:11:51.471
I don't have any college training.

00:11:51.471 --> 00:11:54.236
But I met a high school teacher
who one day changed my life.

00:11:54.236 --> 00:11:57.007
I was waiting on another
student and when he came in

00:11:57.007 --> 00:11:59.322
he said to me, "Young man, go to the board

00:11:59.322 --> 00:12:01.220
"and write what I'm about to tell you."

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:03.343
And I said, "I can't do that, sir."

00:12:03.343 --> 00:12:04.721
And he said, "Why not?"

00:12:04.721 --> 00:12:06.495
I said, "I'm not one of your students."

00:12:06.495 --> 00:12:08.420
He said, "It doesn't matter.

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:10.534
"Follow my directions now."

00:12:10.534 --> 00:12:12.075
I said, "I can't do that sir."

00:12:12.075 --> 00:12:13.556
He said, "Why not?"

00:12:13.556 --> 00:12:17.691
I said, "Because I'm
educable mentally retarded."

00:12:17.691 --> 00:12:20.353
And he came from behind his
desk and he looked at me.

00:12:20.353 --> 00:12:22.342
He said, "Don't ever say that again.

00:12:22.342 --> 00:12:24.431
"Someone's opinion of you does not have

00:12:24.431 --> 00:12:26.260
"to become your reality."

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:29.368
(audience applause)

00:12:29.368 --> 00:12:31.303
I'm saying this is a time more than ever

00:12:31.303 --> 00:12:35.002
that you want to begin
to inoculate yourself

00:12:35.002 --> 00:12:37.593
with positive words,
coming to conventions,

00:12:37.593 --> 00:12:40.872
showing up for meetings,
being on the calls,

00:12:40.872 --> 00:12:43.949
to make yourself unstoppable.

00:12:43.949 --> 00:12:47.126
To get out of your mind the
polluting negative thoughts

00:12:47.126 --> 00:12:49.827
that's causing most
people to go through life

00:12:49.827 --> 00:12:53.055
being stuck because
they're volunteer victims.

00:12:53.055 --> 00:12:55.756
Somebody said that many
people die at age 25

00:12:55.756 --> 00:12:58.421
and don't get buried until they're 65

00:12:58.421 --> 00:13:02.019
because they got so much
garbage in their minds.

00:13:02.019 --> 00:13:06.036
You're here because you got a
clear vision of what you want

00:13:06.036 --> 00:13:07.368
and where you're going.

00:13:07.368 --> 00:13:09.077
Give yourselves a round of applause.

00:13:09.077 --> 00:13:10.827
Come on, bring the energy level up.

00:13:10.827 --> 00:13:11.710
(audience applause)

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:12.543
Yes. Yes.

00:13:14.843 --> 00:13:16.010
You want more.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.257
You want more.

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:23.267
You're different.

00:13:25.171 --> 00:13:28.495
You're different than everybody else.

00:13:28.495 --> 00:13:29.884
Don't worry if they don't get it.

00:13:29.884 --> 00:13:32.930
Don't try and convince
people to do this business.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:34.686
A person convinced against their will

00:13:34.686 --> 00:13:36.601
is of the same opinion still.

00:13:36.601 --> 00:13:39.743
You are not like everybody else.

00:13:39.743 --> 00:13:42.944
You can walk outside and find
pigeons but if you're looking

00:13:42.944 --> 00:13:45.293
for eagles, it's going
to take you a minute.

00:13:45.293 --> 00:13:46.704
You are different.

00:13:46.704 --> 00:13:48.889
It's lonely at the top.

00:13:48.889 --> 00:13:50.373
How many of you know
it's lonely at the top.

00:13:50.373 --> 00:13:51.517
Raise your hands.

00:13:51.517 --> 00:13:54.691
It's lonely at the top but you eat better.

00:13:54.691 --> 00:13:57.925
That's what I'm talking about.

00:13:57.925 --> 00:13:59.140
You're different.

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:00.246
One great entrepreneur said,

00:14:00.246 --> 00:14:01.694
"I choose not to be a common man.

00:14:01.694 --> 00:14:03.611
"It's my right to be uncommon, if I can.

00:14:03.611 --> 00:14:05.529
"I seek opportunity not security.

00:14:05.529 --> 00:14:08.959
"I do not wish to be a kept
citizen humbled and dulled

00:14:08.959 --> 00:14:10.516
"by having the state look after me.

00:14:10.516 --> 00:14:14.009
"I want to take the calculated
risk to dream and to build,

00:14:14.009 --> 00:14:15.466
"to fail and to succeed.

00:14:15.466 --> 00:14:17.446
"I refuse to live from hand to mouth.

00:14:17.446 --> 00:14:19.876
"I prefer the challenges of life

00:14:19.876 --> 00:14:22.078
"to the guaranteed existence,
the thrill of fulfillment

00:14:22.078 --> 00:14:23.972
"to the still calm of utopia.

00:14:23.972 --> 00:14:26.003
"I will never cower before any master,

00:14:26.003 --> 00:14:28.335
"nor bend to any threat.

00:14:28.335 --> 00:14:31.718
"It's my heritage to stand
erect, proud and unafraid,

00:14:31.718 --> 00:14:35.688
"to face the world boldly
and say, this I have done."

00:14:35.688 --> 00:14:38.035
You showed up because
you're building a business

00:14:38.035 --> 00:14:40.285
that you can stand and say,

00:14:40.285 --> 00:14:41.676
I did this.

00:14:41.676 --> 00:14:42.593
I did this.

00:14:43.684 --> 00:14:44.759
This is my dream.

00:14:44.759 --> 00:14:47.217
Give yourselves a round of applause.

00:14:47.217 --> 00:14:49.108
(audience applause)

00:14:49.108 --> 00:14:50.691
Yes. Yes. Yes. Yes.

00:14:53.378 --> 00:14:56.454
It's hard changing your life.

00:14:56.454 --> 00:15:00.605
It was hard when just over three years ago

00:15:00.605 --> 00:15:02.872
in the Penobscot Building
in Detroit, Michigan,

00:15:02.872 --> 00:15:06.427
where I was operating my business,

00:15:06.427 --> 00:15:08.554
and I fell on some hard times

00:15:08.554 --> 00:15:12.036
and I was sleeping in my office.

00:15:12.036 --> 00:15:15.095
It was hard coming into the
lobby and the security said,

00:15:15.095 --> 00:15:17.770
"Excuse me, Mr. Brown, can
we see you for a moment?"

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:18.703
And I said, "Yes."

00:15:18.703 --> 00:15:21.929
And I walked up to the counter
and he gave me an envelope,

00:15:21.929 --> 00:15:25.131
and he said, "Would you
mind reading it here?"

00:15:25.131 --> 00:15:26.967
And I opened the envelope and the envelope

00:15:26.967 --> 00:15:28.854
was from management that said,

00:15:28.854 --> 00:15:32.437
"This is an office
tower, it's not a hotel.

00:15:34.471 --> 00:15:37.554
"Please do not sleep in your office."

00:15:38.811 --> 00:15:41.925
And I said, "Excuse me,
sir, I just work long hours

00:15:41.925 --> 00:15:43.832
"in creating my business.

00:15:43.832 --> 00:15:48.116
"I'm an entrepreneur and right
now things are bad for me,

00:15:48.116 --> 00:15:52.142
"but they're not going
to be this way always.

00:15:52.142 --> 00:15:55.295
"And I just ask for the
opportunity to continue

00:15:55.295 --> 00:15:57.400
"to operate like I'm doing.

00:15:57.400 --> 00:16:00.122
"I'm not trying to make this my home."

00:16:00.122 --> 00:16:02.218
And it was hard coming through the lobby,

00:16:02.218 --> 00:16:03.433
and sometimes they would laugh,

00:16:03.433 --> 00:16:05.738
"There's the guy talking
about becoming successful

00:16:05.738 --> 00:16:06.960
"and look at him.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:11.616
"He's bathing in the bathroom
upstairs on the 21st floor.

00:16:11.616 --> 00:16:13.585
"He sleeps on the floor.

00:16:13.585 --> 00:16:15.882
"Him and two other dreamers up there.

00:16:15.882 --> 00:16:17.516
"Look at him."

00:16:17.516 --> 00:16:19.694
It was hard, ladies and gentlemen.

00:16:19.694 --> 00:16:22.279
Coming to speak to people and I was

00:16:22.279 --> 00:16:25.683
facing financial
difficulties in my own life.

00:16:25.683 --> 00:16:27.624
I was behind on my bills and my dreams

00:16:27.624 --> 00:16:31.001
and I'm saying to them,
"You can live your dream."

00:16:31.001 --> 00:16:32.989
It was hard, ladies and gentlemen.

00:16:32.989 --> 00:16:36.264
It was very difficult to
pick myself up each day

00:16:36.264 --> 00:16:38.057
believing that I could do it.

00:16:38.057 --> 00:16:40.236
There were times that I doubted myself.

00:16:40.236 --> 00:16:43.258
I'd say, "God, why is
this happening to me?

00:16:43.258 --> 00:16:45.795
"I'm just trying to take care
of my children and my mother.

00:16:45.795 --> 00:16:50.068
"I'm not trying to steal
or rob from anybody.

00:16:50.068 --> 00:16:53.258
"Why did this have to happen to me?"

00:16:53.258 --> 00:16:55.245
It was very hard,

00:16:55.245 --> 00:16:57.470
and here's what I want to say to you.

00:16:57.470 --> 00:17:01.813
For those of you that have
experienced some hardships,

00:17:01.813 --> 00:17:04.049
don't give up on your dream.

00:17:04.049 --> 00:17:07.242
No one could have
convinced me by holding on,

00:17:07.242 --> 00:17:10.375
by continuing to push forward,

00:17:10.375 --> 00:17:13.913
by continuing to run toward my dream,

00:17:13.913 --> 00:17:17.496
that one day I would
have my own talk show.

00:17:18.862 --> 00:17:20.258
It's a long shot, ladies and gentlemen,

00:17:20.258 --> 00:17:23.124
from Liberty City in an
abandoned building on a floor,

00:17:23.124 --> 00:17:25.611
never knowing my mother or father.

00:17:25.611 --> 00:17:28.429
It's a long shot being here with you today

00:17:28.429 --> 00:17:30.717
in this dome in Atlanta.

00:17:30.717 --> 00:17:33.199
It's a long shot, no college training,

00:17:33.199 --> 00:17:34.858
labeled educable mentally retarded,

00:17:34.858 --> 00:17:37.433
but I kept running toward my dream.

00:17:37.433 --> 00:17:40.433
(audience applause)

00:17:44.798 --> 00:17:45.715
Don't stop.

00:17:51.905 --> 00:17:53.423
Don't stop.

00:17:53.423 --> 00:17:56.423
(audience applause)

00:18:07.102 --> 00:18:10.185
Don't stop running toward your dream.

00:18:11.372 --> 00:18:13.199
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:18:13.199 --> 00:18:17.080
I made this video because
Demo Healthcare asked me to.

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.265
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:18:18.265 --> 00:18:20.094
that you want me to profile next,

00:18:20.094 --> 00:18:22.965
leave it in the comments below
and I'll see what I can do.

00:18:22.965 --> 00:18:25.817
I'd also love to know what
of Les Brown's top 10 rules

00:18:25.817 --> 00:18:27.626
hit you the hardest.

00:18:27.626 --> 00:18:29.660
He's one of my favorite
speakers so I'd love to know

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:32.019
which of the 10 points
meant the most to you.

00:18:32.019 --> 00:18:34.584
Leave it in the comments below
and I'll join the discussion.

00:18:34.584 --> 00:18:36.275
Thank you so much for watching.

00:18:36.275 --> 00:18:39.775
Continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

00:18:44.916 --> 00:18:46.936
- Program your mind deliberately.

00:18:46.936 --> 00:18:50.422
The reason that most people
don't achieve their goals

00:18:50.422 --> 00:18:54.141
is because they are thinking
like everybody else.

00:18:54.141 --> 00:18:58.368
16 revolutionary words, "Be
not conformed to this world,

00:18:58.368 --> 00:19:02.284
"be transformed by the
renewing of your mind."

00:19:02.284 --> 00:19:04.451
That's an ongoing process.

00:19:05.398 --> 00:19:06.231
What are your goals?

00:19:06.231 --> 00:19:07.187
What are your dreams?

00:19:07.187 --> 00:19:09.951
Nightingale was right, "You
don't get in life what you want.

00:19:09.951 --> 00:19:11.824
"You get in life what you are."

00:19:11.824 --> 00:19:15.361
And so you want to take the
time every day to listen

00:19:15.361 --> 00:19:19.114
to things that can help to
program your mind positively.

00:19:19.114 --> 00:19:20.833
Because at the end of the day,

00:19:20.833 --> 00:19:25.090
if you don't program your mind
it's going to be programmed.

00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:26.100
Trust me.

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:27.907
It's going to be bombarded with all kind

00:19:27.907 --> 00:19:29.556
of head trash, commercials.

00:19:29.556 --> 00:19:31.867
I was at a service station pumping gas

00:19:31.867 --> 00:19:33.722
and a commercial came up.

00:19:33.722 --> 00:19:37.134
You get on the elevator
and commercials are there.

00:19:37.134 --> 00:19:39.707
You look at billboards, there
are messages just coming in,

00:19:39.707 --> 00:19:43.624
over 5,000, 10,000 messages
on a regular basis.

00:19:45.851 --> 00:19:48.477
And so as you look at
your goals and dreams,

00:19:48.477 --> 00:19:51.078
it's very important
that you are intentional

00:19:51.078 --> 00:19:54.745
about controlling what
goes on in your mind.

00:19:56.175 --> 00:19:58.845
Because everything gets
in through the eyes,

00:19:58.845 --> 00:20:00.595
and through the ears.

00:20:01.736 --> 00:20:03.617
So what do you want?

00:20:03.617 --> 00:20:04.714
What do you want for yourself?

00:20:04.714 --> 00:20:07.585
What I'm doing right now, I
didn't do it for 14 years.

00:20:07.585 --> 00:20:08.585
You know why?

00:20:08.585 --> 00:20:13.326
Because I was suffering
from possibility blindness.

00:20:13.326 --> 00:20:14.884
Have you ever thought
about doing something

00:20:14.884 --> 00:20:18.159
and you looked at what you
wanted to do and your heart said,

00:20:18.159 --> 00:20:19.951
"I can do that."

00:20:19.951 --> 00:20:22.325
And then your mind asked, "How?"

00:20:22.325 --> 00:20:26.926
Then you start thinking,
"Well, I can't do that.

00:20:26.926 --> 00:20:29.329
"I don't have a college education.

00:20:29.329 --> 00:20:30.445
"I can't do that.

00:20:30.445 --> 00:20:33.063
'I don't have an MBA or PhD.

00:20:33.063 --> 00:20:34.666
"I can't do that.

00:20:34.666 --> 00:20:37.419
"I've never worked for
a major corporation.

00:20:37.419 --> 00:20:40.742
"Why would corporations
reach over people with PhDs

00:20:40.742 --> 00:20:43.198
"and MBAs and years of
experience and pay me

00:20:43.198 --> 00:20:45.783
"to come in to do
something I've never done?

00:20:45.783 --> 00:20:49.466
I thought about doing this for years

00:20:49.466 --> 00:20:51.966
and I talked myself out of it.

00:20:53.614 --> 00:20:55.195
There's an African proverb that says,

00:20:55.195 --> 00:20:57.601
"If there's no enemy within,

00:20:57.601 --> 00:21:01.490
"the enemy outside can do us no harm."

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.442
Shakespeare says, "Therefore,
dear Brutus, it's not

00:21:03.442 --> 00:21:07.609
"in our stars, but in ourselves
that we are underlings."

00:21:09.068 --> 00:21:11.074
And so as you look at yourself
and look at your goals

00:21:11.074 --> 00:21:13.783
and look at your dreams, I'm saying to you

00:21:13.783 --> 00:21:16.061
that it's possible.

00:21:16.061 --> 00:21:20.282
Because if anybody at any
point in time had a goal,

00:21:20.282 --> 00:21:22.772
had a dream of what
they wanted to achieve,

00:21:22.772 --> 00:21:26.355
and they made it happen,
then it's possible

00:21:27.247 --> 00:21:28.995
that you can do it too.

00:21:28.995 --> 00:21:30.191
But you've got to be intentional

00:21:30.191 --> 00:21:31.927
about programming your mind.

00:21:31.927 --> 00:21:35.969
It's necessary that
you detoxify your life,

00:21:35.969 --> 00:21:37.803
that you have to look at your life,

00:21:37.803 --> 00:21:40.110
and look at the people in your life.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:41.979
And Jim Rowan said ask the question,

00:21:41.979 --> 00:21:45.182
"What is this relationship doing to me?"

00:21:45.182 --> 00:21:47.082
See most people never live their dreams

00:21:47.082 --> 00:21:51.042
because they are saddled with
too many toxic, negative,

00:21:51.042 --> 00:21:54.209
energy-draining people in their lives.

00:21:56.367 --> 00:22:00.825
Look at the people around you
and ask, "Is this relationship

00:22:00.825 --> 00:22:04.325
"helping me to grow mentally, emotionally,

00:22:06.073 --> 00:22:08.763
"financially, spiritually."

00:22:08.763 --> 00:22:10.806
And the financial part, MIT did a study,

00:22:10.806 --> 00:22:13.100
you earn within two to
three thousand dollars

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:15.576
of your closest friends.

00:22:15.576 --> 00:22:18.629
It's necessary if you are
serious about your dream

00:22:18.629 --> 00:22:21.170
that you detoxify your life.

00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:23.053
Dr. Dennis Kimbro out of Atlanta said,

00:22:23.053 --> 00:22:25.710
"If you are the smartest
one in your group,

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:28.210
"you need to get a new group."

00:22:29.924 --> 00:22:34.705
When I heard that, I got all
the broke people out my life.

00:22:34.705 --> 00:22:37.469
Why, because people rub off on you.

00:22:37.469 --> 00:22:41.526
John H. Johnson, who had a
loan of $500 from his mother

00:22:41.526 --> 00:22:45.361
and built a 400 million dollar empire

00:22:45.361 --> 00:22:49.528
with Ebony magazine and Jet
magazine fired his best friend.

00:22:50.553 --> 00:22:52.832
And the reporter asked, "Why'd
you fire your best friend?"

00:22:52.832 --> 00:22:54.253
He said, "He told me I couldn't do it."

00:22:54.253 --> 00:22:56.377
He said, "Hell, I didn't
think I could do it.

00:22:56.377 --> 00:22:59.338
"I didn't need anybody on
my payroll to tell me."

00:22:59.338 --> 00:23:00.235
(laughs)

00:23:00.235 --> 00:23:03.188
And so you have to look
at your life and say,

00:23:03.188 --> 00:23:06.688
"Hey who's in my circle, who's in my ear?"

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:10.506
The only reason that most
of us don't accumulate

00:23:10.506 --> 00:23:13.738
a level of achievement in our lives,

00:23:13.738 --> 00:23:16.287
one, most people end up aiming low.

00:23:16.287 --> 00:23:18.336
That's what I did most of my life.

00:23:18.336 --> 00:23:20.102
Most people fail in life

00:23:20.102 --> 00:23:21.609
not because they aim too high and miss.

00:23:21.609 --> 00:23:25.342
Most people fail in life because
they aim too low and hit.

00:23:25.342 --> 00:23:26.575
And that's what I did.

00:23:26.575 --> 00:23:27.680
I was a disc jockey.

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:30.486
I was very satisfied
I had achieved a level

00:23:30.486 --> 00:23:32.868
of professionalism and
mastery in that area.

00:23:32.868 --> 00:23:35.592
And then someone challenged me
and said, "You can do more."

00:23:35.592 --> 00:23:38.694
And it took him 14 years to convince me

00:23:38.694 --> 00:23:41.194
to become this person that you now see.

00:23:41.194 --> 00:23:42.727
This person that you now see,

00:23:42.727 --> 00:23:45.314
this voice which I
consider my power voice,

00:23:45.314 --> 00:23:50.101
I had absolutely no idea
that this person existed.

00:23:50.101 --> 00:23:53.600
But there's some times in
life someone can take you

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:56.837
to a place within yourself
where you can never go

00:23:56.837 --> 00:23:59.462
by yourself, and he saw something in me.

00:23:59.462 --> 00:24:02.596
And sometimes you have to
believe in somebody's belief

00:24:02.596 --> 00:24:05.252
in you until your belief kicks in.

